00:33:57.271 --> 00:33:59.941
groomed you. plied you
with alcohol and drugs.

754
00:34:00.008 --> 00:34:03.711
and touched you sexually.
that was a lie?

755
00:34:03.845 --> 00:34:05.078
- Yeah.

756
00:34:05.145 --> 00:34:06.814
- And when you told them
that you believed

757
00:34:06.915 --> 00:34:08.315
Clint O'Neill killed
Ian Larkin--

758
00:34:08.415 --> 00:34:10.250
- I was lying.

759
00:34:12.554 --> 00:34:13.721
- Or you're lying now.

760
00:34:13.788 --> 00:34:16.423
- Mr. Carisi.

761
00:34:16.490 --> 00:34:21.896
- Mr. Ray. why would
you lie to the police?

762
00:34:21.996 --> 00:34:23.598
- They said Ian was dead.

763
00:34:23.665 --> 00:34:25.165
I felt terrible.

764
00:34:25.299 --> 00:34:27.569
I told them what I thought
they wanted to hear.

765
00:34:27.669 --> 00:34:31.906
But being here now in
the court. I can't do it.

766
00:34:32.006 --> 00:34:33.608
I gotta tell the truth.

767
00:35:03.571 --> 00:35:04.839
- Hey. Ray.

768
00:35:04.939 --> 00:35:06.808
Closing doors in 45. okay?

769
00:35:06.908 --> 00:35:08.743
- Yeah.

770
00:35:08.810 --> 00:35:12.312
- I just saw
Sharon Huntsinger outside. huh?

771
00:35:12.379 --> 00:35:14.649
I'm assuming she's
here to see you.

772
00:35:14.716 --> 00:35:16.084
- She might have said hello.

773
00:35:16.183 --> 00:35:17.384
She's a fan of my work.

774
00:35:17.451 --> 00:35:20.021
- Ah. is that what
you're going with?

775
00:35:20.054 --> 00:35:21.656
- Why is that so
hard to believe?

776
00:35:23.625 --> 00:35:25.827
- What'd she give you?

777
00:35:25.860 --> 00:35:27.996
What?
- Contract to be a client.

778
00:35:28.029 --> 00:35:30.865
She's going to book
me some gigs in Japan.

779
00:35:30.932 --> 00:35:34.434
- Was it worth it?

780
00:35:34.501 --> 00:35:36.004
Was it?

781
00:35:36.037 --> 00:35:37.505
- What do you want me to say?

782
00:35:37.572 --> 00:35:42.010
- I want you to tell me how you
can let someone like O'Neill

783
00:35:42.076 --> 00:35:46.014
get away with
what they did to you.

784
00:35:46.114 --> 00:35:48.516
with what they did to Ian.

785
00:35:51.085 --> 00:35:52.620
- Ian is gone. all right?

786
00:35:52.687 --> 00:35:54.154
I'm here.

787
00:35:54.254 --> 00:35:56.456
I've been living
with this for 20 years.

788
00:35:56.524 --> 00:35:58.225
Do you know what I have
to show for it?

789
00:35:58.291 --> 00:36:01.629
Pain. poverty.

790
00:36:01.696 --> 00:36:04.164
These. this is it.

791
00:36:06.000 --> 00:36:08.168
Clock's running out.

792
00:36:08.268 --> 00:36:10.437
It's my last chance.
And you know what?

793
00:36:10.538 --> 00:36:13.775
If Ian were here.
he'd understand.

794
00:36:26.253 --> 00:36:28.856
- I feel bad for what
happened to that kid.

795
00:36:28.956 --> 00:36:30.190
I do.

796
00:36:30.223 --> 00:36:31.592
But I didn't know him.

797
00:36:31.659 --> 00:36:34.629
And I had nothing
to do with his death.

798
00:36:34.696 --> 00:36:37.932
- Why do you think
Mr. Larkin was fixated on you?

799
00:36:37.965 --> 00:36:40.333
- Well. I can't say for sure.

800
00:36:40.367 --> 00:36:43.370
but I've been fighting
a long time.

801
00:36:43.470 --> 00:36:45.673
lots of states.
lots of cities.

802
00:36:45.773 --> 00:36:48.576
And everywhere I went.
people always wanted

803
00:36:48.643 --> 00:36:49.844
something from me.

804
00:36:49.944 --> 00:36:54.214
wanted me to be their hero.
their dad. their teacher.

805
00:36:54.281 --> 00:36:59.386
But in this case.
I suppose I'm their monster.

806
00:36:59.486 --> 00:37:02.557
But they got the wrong guy.

807
00:37:02.657 --> 00:37:03.991
- Nothing further.

808
00:37:12.166 --> 00:37:14.334
- You good at your job.
Mr. O'Neill?

809
00:37:14.434 --> 00:37:16.671
- I'm a ten-time champ.

810
00:37:16.704 --> 00:37:18.039
You tell me.

811
00:37:18.106 --> 00:37:20.373
- How many of those belts were
in professional boxing?

812
00:37:20.474 --> 00:37:21.542
- Two.

813
00:37:21.642 --> 00:37:24.344
- And since then.
you've fought exclusively

814
00:37:24.411 --> 00:37:27.314
for Bruiser Fighting
Championship. correct?

815
00:37:27.380 --> 00:37:29.851
- Yep. bigger
and better things.

816
00:37:29.917 --> 00:37:31.753
- It wasn't because
you were permanently banned

817
00:37:31.819 --> 00:37:36.224
from boxing in 1992.
accused of taking a dive.

818
00:37:36.256 --> 00:37:38.192
if I'm not mistaken?

819
00:37:38.291 --> 00:37:39.694
- If you say so.

820
00:37:39.761 --> 00:37:41.596
- Well. to be fair.
I'm not saying that.

821
00:37:41.696 --> 00:37:44.732
That's every sanctioning
body in pro boxing.

822
00:37:44.832 --> 00:37:47.235
the WBC. the IBF. the WBA.

823
00:37:47.267 --> 00:37:48.569
- Your point is?

824
00:37:48.636 --> 00:37:51.404
- Well. Mr. O'Neill.
I just find it interesting

825
00:37:51.506 --> 00:37:55.710
that you claim success because
of your skill in the ring.

826
00:37:55.810 --> 00:37:58.112
But who's to say. given
your history of cheating.

827
00:37:58.179 --> 00:37:59.814
that any of your fights
were on the level?

828
00:37:59.914 --> 00:38:03.084
I mean. doesn't it call into
question your entire career?

829
00:38:03.184 --> 00:38:04.986
- No.

830
00:38:05.019 --> 00:38:06.353
I wouldn't say that.

831
00:38:06.419 --> 00:38:07.454
- Of course you
wouldn't say that.

832
00:38:07.487 --> 00:38:09.190
You've got a legacy to protect.

833
00:38:09.223 --> 00:38:12.960
But to the rest of us.
your willingness to lie.

834
00:38:13.027 --> 00:38:14.294
to betray the sport

835
00:38:14.394 --> 00:38:16.296
that supposedly you care
so much about--

836
00:38:16.363 --> 00:38:19.634
- I have given my life
to this business.

837
00:38:19.667 --> 00:38:22.469
- But who's to say any
of your fights were real?

838
00:38:22.503 --> 00:38:24.539
All your knockouts. your wins--

839
00:38:24.639 --> 00:38:27.008
how do we know that those guys
weren't taking dives for you?

840
00:38:27.108 --> 00:38:29.510
- You wouldn't last ten seconds

841
00:38:29.610 --> 00:38:31.179
with the men I faced.
- Oh. please.

842
00:38:31.279 --> 00:38:32.847
We all know you
don't fight real men.

843
00:38:32.914 --> 00:38:34.015
- Is that so?

844
00:38:34.115 --> 00:38:35.283
- Objection. Badgering.

845
00:38:35.348 --> 00:38:36.951
- No. no. You're out hurting
teenage boys.

846
00:38:37.051 --> 00:38:38.318
- Sustained.
Mr. Carisi.

847
00:38:38.418 --> 00:38:40.254
- Shut your mouth.

848
00:38:40.288 --> 00:38:42.056
- Is that what you tell
the children you molest?

849
00:38:42.123 --> 00:38:43.658
- Enough.

850
00:38:46.393 --> 00:38:50.031
Do you have any pertinent
questions left. Mr. Carisi?

851
00:38:53.868 --> 00:38:56.436
- No. Your Honor.

852
00:38:56.537 --> 00:38:58.172
I have nothing further.

853
00:39:06.881 --> 00:39:10.151
- As to the count of
murder in the second degree.

854
00:39:10.251 --> 00:39:12.220
how do you find?

855
00:39:12.286 --> 00:39:15.056
- We find the defendant
not guilty.

856
00:39:19.426 --> 00:39:21.394
- Ladies and gentlemen.
I know this has been

857
00:39:21.461 --> 00:39:23.430
a lengthy and
difficult deliberation.

858
00:39:23.496 --> 00:39:24.665
Personally.
along with the State.

859
00:39:24.765 --> 00:39:26.067
I thank you for your service.

860
00:39:37.011 --> 00:39:39.780
- Hey. I know that it's not
the verdict that we wanted.

861
00:39:39.847 --> 00:39:42.650
so let's take the night
to be pissed.

862
00:39:42.717 --> 00:39:46.354
But tomorrow morning.
we start to build a new case.

863
00:39:46.419 --> 00:39:48.055
- O'Neill was acquitted. boss.

864
00:39:48.155 --> 00:39:50.224
- Of murder.
not of sexual assault.

865
00:39:50.324 --> 00:39:51.926
- Do you really think
we can get enough on him

866
00:39:51.993 --> 00:39:53.426
without Ian or Razor?

867
00:39:53.527 --> 00:39:55.495
- I think that Clint O'Neill
has been out there.

868
00:39:55.563 --> 00:39:57.665
He's been a predator
for a very long time.

869
00:39:57.698 --> 00:40:00.001
There has to be other victims.

870
00:40:00.101 --> 00:40:01.802
We just need to find them.

871
00:40:01.836 --> 00:40:03.604
- It's going to be
an uphill battle.

872
00:40:03.671 --> 00:40:05.740
- Yeah. so we widen the net.

873
00:40:05.806 --> 00:40:07.875
We talk to every
single person that

874
00:40:07.942 --> 00:40:10.278
has crossed paths
with Clint O'Neill

875
00:40:10.311 --> 00:40:11.478
in the last 20 years.

876
00:40:11.545 --> 00:40:14.248
But we do whatever it takes.

877
00:40:14.282 --> 00:40:15.415
- The fight goes on.

878
00:40:15.516 --> 00:40:18.085
- Captain Benson.
message for you.

879
00:40:27.395 --> 00:40:29.530
- Thank you.
Excuse me.

880
00:40:29.630 --> 00:40:30.798
Hey.

881
00:40:30.865 --> 00:40:32.900
- Old fella was jumped
as he left the diner.

882
00:40:32.934 --> 00:40:35.269
stabbed to death.
choked on his own blood.

883
00:40:39.340 --> 00:40:41.075
Rough way to go.

884
00:40:44.078 --> 00:40:46.047
- Is the attacker in custody?

885
00:40:46.080 --> 00:40:47.315
- Back of the squad car.

886
00:40:56.691 --> 00:40:57.825
- Shawn?

887
00:41:00.094 --> 00:41:02.029
- I had to do something.

887
